# The fixture PDFs are hand-built, uncompressed and pure ASCII - they contain no
# NUL byte, so git's heuristic reads them as text. With core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows a checkout would then rewrite their line endings, and a PDF's xref
# table is a list of byte offsets, so every one of them would be wrong. Marking
# them binary is what keeps a clone of this repo byte-identical to the commit.
#
# The suffixes beyond .pdf are here for Phase 2 rather than for anything present
# today, and mirror the list the vault's own .gitattributes needs.
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.doc binary
*.xls binary
*.heic binary
